From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] dts: assert display power from the expander

The panel rail is enabled by XL9555 P07 and nothing else. Until now Linux read
that pin's state and left it alone, which works only because the ESP-IDF
firmware drove it before handing over -- the expander stays powered across an
ESP32 reset. On a cold boot (battery pulled) the PCA9555 powers up with every
pin an input, DISP_EN is not driven, and the AMOLED stays dark.

Modelling it as a regulator-fixed is what makes the kernel assert it. There is
no CO5300 driver yet, so nothing consumes the supply; the point is the enable.

    display_vcc: regulator-display {
        compatible = "regulator-fixed";
        regulator-name = "display";
        regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
        regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
        enable-active-high;
        gpio = <&xl9555 7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
        regulator-always-on;
        regulator-boot-on;
    };

gpio 7 on the expander is P07 -- the chip reported as gpiochip625 with 16
lines, and the driver numbers P00..P07 = 0..7, P10..P17 = 8..15.

regulator-always-on and regulator-boot-on so the rail comes up during boot and
is not gated on a consumer existing.

NOT YET VERIFIED ON HARDWARE. The kernel builds and boots with this node, but
whether /sys/class/regulator shows the supply enabled, and whether the pin is
actually driven, still needs checking. Recorded here rather than claimed.

--- a/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-devkit-c1.dts
+++ b/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-devkit-c1.dts
@@ -66,6 +66,30 @@
 			};
 		};
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Display power, as a switchable regulator on the expander.
+	 *
+	 * The panel rail is enabled by XL9555 P07 and nothing else. There is no
+	 * CO5300 driver yet, but modelling the enable here is what makes the
+	 * kernel ASSERT it. Without it the pin keeps whatever state the
+	 * previous firmware left: harmless across a warm reset, wrong on a
+	 * cold boot, where the PCA9555 powers up all-inputs and the AMOLED
+	 * stays dark.
+	 *
+	 * gpio 7 on the expander is P07 (linear numbering: P00..P07 = 0..7,
+	 * P10..P17 = 8..15).
+	 */
+	display_vcc: regulator-display {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+		regulator-name = "display";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		gpio = <&xl9555 7 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
 };
 
 &iomux {
